\fs24 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 description: 
\f1\fs26 Why do we seek out rituals, and what happens when we adopt practices that originate elsewhere? Chaga Chaga considers ritual as something fluid: translated, adapted and reshaped through use. Rather than treating cultural forms as fixed or pure, the project asks how new rituals might emerge through conscious recomposition. A Chaga tea ritual serves as its starting point, bringing together objects, gestures and forms of interaction to create a new material framework for gathering, preparing and sharing.
